# Docker build-context exclusions.
#
# Docker matches these patterns against the CONTEXT-RELATIVE path and
# ANCHORS EVERY PATTERN AT THE CONTEXT ROOT: a pattern without a slash
# (`__pycache__`) matches only `<root>/__pycache__`, never
# `<root>/contracts/__pycache__`. Nested copies must therefore be written
# with an explicit `**/` prefix. `*` does not cross a path separator, `**` does.
# The last matching rule wins, so a later `!pattern` re-includes a path.
# The rules below are verified by tests/judge/test_docker_hardening.py and by
# `python3 tools/container_local_check.py` (effective-context computation).

# VCS metadata and local tool state (any depth).
**/.git
**/.hg
**/.svn
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.tox
**/.ipynb_checkpoints
**/node_modules
**/*.egg-info

# Generated evidence is produced inside the container, never baked into the image.
artifacts/reports/latest/*.json
artifacts/reports/latest/*.html
artifacts/reports/latest/*.txt
artifacts/reports/latest/*.csv
artifacts/reports/latest/*.md
artifacts/reports/doc_claims/
artifacts/reports/release/
# The published trajectory log is generated by `make official-eval`; the offline
# check deliberately runs without it so a run proves it produces its own outputs.
artifacts/trajectories/

# Sealed truth must never enter the image (REQ-SEAL-001, D-16-02).
# `episodes/*/sealed/` does NOT cover the real depth-2 layout
# (episodes/dev/<episode>/sealed/), so every depth is listed explicitly.
episodes/sealed/
episodes/*/sealed/
episodes/*/*/sealed/
episodes/hidden/

# Secrets and key material (any depth).
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/id_rsa
**/id_ed25519
